cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository together with the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "The Ford–Johnson algorithm, no longer unbeaten for less than 47 elements"
abstract: >-
  Paper, complete comparison trees, and Lean 4 formalisation proving that
  26 elements can be sorted in at most 90 comparisons and 46 elements in
  at most 194 comparisons. The one-comparison saving over Ford–Johnson
  extends throughout 26–32 and 46–64 elements. The code, scripts, and
  certificate data are licensed under Apache 2.0; the paper (note.tex and
  note.pdf) is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
authors:
  - family-names: "Sager"
    given-names: "H. G."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3916-9042"
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23645924
